Z||000000||Fiero54||03-10-2001||09:53 PM||||I'm wondering if has or has seen scoops for notchback fieros that mount where the cover panels are next to the deck lid, and they wrap over the notchback. <BR>||||reg||9
Z||000001||Formula88||03-10-2001||09:58 PM||||I've seen then on a car, but not for sale anywhere.  They look kinda neat, but don't forget, those engine vents are to let air OUT, not take it in, so you're changine the ventilation in your engine compartment.  Heat's a big concern in that engine compartment, so let the buyer beware.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||03-11-2001||11:43 PM||||These??<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lazycscoops_1.jpg"> <P>If so they are "F.O.C.O.A. Lazy C Air Vent Scoops"<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroowners.com/store1.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroowners.com/store1.htm</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">  </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>PFF Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1431213" TARGET=_blank><BR>Photopoint Gallery (Updated Weekly)</A>||||reg||5
Z||000003||firstfiero||03-12-2001||06:54 AM||||   anybody have a picture of what they look like installed? Do they make a noticeable difference in your performance? ||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||03-12-2001||10:39 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by firstfiero:<BR><B> Do they make a noticeable difference in your performance? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I dont think that they would unless you actually plumbed them into the intake for a ram air setup.  And if you are looking at performance by means of cooling the engine down, I dont know how well that will work.  Like Forumula88 said, heat is meant to come out.  If you used those scoops to force more air through the engine, you will be working against the convection currents already present.  You'd be trying to force air out the bottom of the engine or out somewhere else.<P>Just my opinion, I personally wouldnt do it.<P><P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
